8,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,2629,315,279,6169,3429,41214,315,220,16,23,374,220,17,16,13,3555,374,279,2629,315,279,6169,3429,41214,315,220,16,24,23,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe sum of the proper divisors of 18 is 21. What is the sum of the proper divisors of 198?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"863695a3a671e1c942f59f7df8e4b720f355d9512f40fed87b7dab8b135c451c"},"seconds":12.108371496200562,"seed":689733084465942213,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the sum of the proper divisors of 198, we need to first determine all the proper divisors of 198 and then sum them up. Proper divisors of a number are all the divisors of that number excluding the number itself.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorization of 198:\n\\[ 198 = 2 \\times 99 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 33 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 11 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 11. \\]\n\nNext, we list all the divisors of 198. Using the prime factorization, the divisors are:\n\\[ 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 11, 18, 22, 33, 66, 99, 198. \\]\n\nThe proper divisors are all the divisors except 198 itself:\n\\[ 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 11, 18, 22, 33, 66, 99. \\]\n\nNow, we sum these proper divisors:\n\\[ 1 + 2 + 3 + 6 + 9 + 11 + 18 + 22 + 33 + 66 + 99. \\]\n\nWe can add these step by step:\n\\[ 1 + 2 = 3, \\]\n\\[ 3 + 3 = 6, \\]\n\\[ 6 + 6 = 12, \\]\n\\[ 12 + 9 = 21, \\]\n\\[ 21 + 11 = 32, \\]\n\\[ 32 + 18 = 50, \\]\n\\[ 50 + 22 = 72, \\]\n\\[ 72 + 33 = 105, \\]\n\\[ 105 + 66 = 171, \\]\n\\[ 171 + 99 = 270. \\]\n\nThus, the sum of the proper divisors of 198 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{270}. \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{270}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"number_theory:270"}
